## Summary

Both files implement a High Level Emulation (HLE) of the KN5000 control panel serial protocol. Key aspects:

**Serial Protocol Features:**
- 2-byte command structure from main CPU
- Bit-banged synchronous serial using SIOCLK (clock) and RXD/TXD (data)
- Rising edge samples RXD, falling edge outputs TXD
- Pre-output of bit 0 on send_byte() with special handling of first falling edge

**Command Types:**
- Initialization commands (0x1f, 0x1d, 0x1e, 0xdd)
- Query commands (0x20, 0xe0 for button segments, LED control)
- LED control commands (rows 0x00-0x0c for right panel, 0xc0-0xc8 for left)

**Button/LED Handling:**
- 11 segments per panel (left/right)
- Segment queries return 8-bit button state bitmaps
- LED commands map directly to MAME output_finder arrays for emulator display

**Sync Protocol:**
- Type 3 sync packet (0x18 0x00) used as acknowledgment for most commands
- Button packets encode panel and segment info in header byte

